  "oral_argument": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "eefc4879d57f4c9c96dc8602e9f3153a9524c4304dfb59196e706765806d64da",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-eefc4879d57f-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Ginsburg, does the law apply only to towing companies that tow and store the automobile, or does it also apply to garages that receive cars for repair?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "eefc4879d57f4c9c96dc8602e9f3153a9524c4304dfb59196e706765806d64da",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-eefc4879d57f-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 6,
              "start": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Breyer, and are all those things preempted? I would be amazed."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "eefc4879d57f4c9c96dc8602e9f3153a9524c4304dfb59196e706765806d64da",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-eefc4879d57f-0000-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 15,
              "start": 15
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Scalia, it includes storage, is that the point you are coming to, right?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "eefc4879d57f4c9c96dc8602e9f3153a9524c4304dfb59196e706765806d64da",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-eefc4879d57f-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Breyer, no, there's a lot of language in the majority pretty much along the line that Justice Scalia said. And not sure if that's your point."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "eefc4879d57f4c9c96dc8602e9f3153a9524c4304dfb59196e706765806d64da",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-eefc4879d57f-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 22,
              "start": 22
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Sotomayor, that's your problem, which is, what is it directed to? And that's the real \u2026"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "eefc4879d57f4c9c96dc8602e9f3153a9524c4304dfb59196e706765806d64da",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-eefc4879d57f-0001-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 27,
              "start": 27
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kagan, suppose the New Hampshire laws were more onerous than they are. Suppose they said to a towing company, once you've towed this car you have to hold on to it forever. Or suppose they said you have to hire private investigators to figure out who owns the car. Would any of those be preempted?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "eefc4879d57f4c9c96dc8602e9f3153a9524c4304dfb59196e706765806d64da",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-eefc4879d57f-0002-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 41,
              "start": 41
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Scalia, i don't understand what you just said. Say it again."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "eefc4879d57f4c9c96dc8602e9f3153a9524c4304dfb59196e706765806d64da",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-eefc4879d57f-0002-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 48,
              "start": 48
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Scalia, so it would depend upon how severe the consumer protection law is, is that right? If it's a consumer protection law that really whacks the tow\u2011truck operator, that would be different from a moderate, benign consumer protection law? We have to examine each consumer protection law on its own, is that it?"
      }
    ],
